title: Proposition 38
---
order: 38
---
short_label: X.38
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a medial rectangle are added together, then the whole is irrational; let it be called the <i>second bimedial</i> straight line.
----
proof:

Let two medial straight lines {AB} and {BC} commensurable in square only and containing a medial rectangle be added together.

I say that {AC} is irrational.

Set out a rational straight line {DE}, and apply parallelogram {DF|DFh} to {DE} equal to the square on {AC}, producing {DG} as breadth. [!just I.41]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.38 diagram" src="propX38.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: AC with B on it, and the parallelogram DF (declared
    // DEFG) applied to the rational line DE with EH (random face) applied
    // inside it, leaving HF. Added, hidden at rest: a solid twin DE
    // (initiallyHidden) so the rational line stands before the
    // parallelogram; transparent targets AB, BC, DG, DH, HG (;0;0;0);
    // faceless, strokeless twins DFh, EHh, HFh that carry the highlights of
    // DF, EH and the remainder HF, so a highlight never raises a face over
    // the figure (#140); prose and captions reach them with the display
    // override ({DF|DFh}, {EH|EHh}, {HF|HFh}). Resting figure unchanged.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C (given), D, E and
    // the offscreen frees. D and E arrive with "Set out a rational straight
    // line DE", so they are deferred; G, F, H are derived and listed per
    // slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","AC","AB","BC"];
    var DES   = GIVEN.concat(["D","E","DE"]);
    var DFS   = DES.concat(["G","F","DEFG","DFh","DG"]);
    var ALL   = DFS.concat(["H","EH","EHh","HFh","DH","HG"]);
