        title: "X.38",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "D0;point;free;40,-1000;0;0",
            "D3;point;free;40,1000;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,40,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,140,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,180,0",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "D;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,0,90",
            "E;point;lineSlider;D0,D3,0,210",
            "DG';line;perpendicular;D,E;0;0;0",
            "G';point;last;DG';0;0",
            "G;point;proportion;D,E,A,C,A,C,D,G'",
            "F;point;parallelogram;E,D,G",
            "DEFG;polygon;quadrilateral;D,E,F,G;0;0;black;random",
            "H';point;proportion;D,E,A,B,A,B,D,G;0;0",
            "H;point;proportion;D,E,B,C,B,C,H',G",
            "EH;polygon;parallelogram;E,D,H;0;0;black;random",
            // Slide-only twin and highlight targets.
            "DE;line;connect;D,E",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C;0;0;0",
            "DG;line;connect;D,G;0;0;0",
            "DH;line;connect;D,H;0;0;0",
            "HG;line;connect;H,G;0;0;0",
            "DFh;polygon;quadrilateral;D,E,F,G;0;0;0;0",
            "EHh;polygon;parallelogram;E,D,H;0;0;0;0",
            "HFh;polygon;parallelogram;H,G,F;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["DE"],
        deferDraggables: ["D","E"],
        slides: [
            { text: "“If two medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a medial rectangle are added together,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.38" }] },
            { text: "then the whole is irrational; let it be called the second bimedial straight line.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC"] },
            { text: "Let two medial straight lines {AB} and {BC} commensurable in square only and containing a medial rectangle be added together.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "I say that {AC} is irrational.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC"] },
            { text: "Set out a rational straight line {DE},",
              visible: DES,
              highlighted: ["DE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "DE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "and apply parallelogram {DF|DFh} to {DE} equal to the square on {AC}, producing {DG} as breadth.",
              visible: DFS,
              highlighted: ["DFh","DE","AC","DG"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "DEFG", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "DF = square on AC", ref: "I.41" }] },
            { text: "Since the square on {AC} equals the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC} and twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC},",
              visible: DFS,
              highlighted: ["AC","AB","BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AC² = AB² + BC² + 2 AB·BC", ref: "II.4" }] },
            { text: "apply {EH|EHh}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC}, to {DE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EHh","AB","BC","DE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EH", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Then the remainder {HF|HFh} equals twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HFh","AB","BC"] },
            { text: "Since each of the straight lines {AB} and {BC} is medial, therefore the squares on {AB} and {BC} are also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "But, by hypothesis, twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "And {EH|EHh} equals the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EHh","AB","BC"] },
            { text: "while {FH|HFh} equals twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HFh","AB","BC"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the rectangles {EH|EHh} and {HF|HFh} is medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EHh","HFh"] },
            { text: "And they are applied to the rational straight line {DE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EHh","HFh","DE"] },
            { text: "therefore each of the straight lines {DH} and {HG} is rational and incommensurable in length with {DE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DH","HG","DE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DH, HG rational, incommensurable in length with DE", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since {AB} is incommensurable in length with {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "and {AB} is to {BC} as the square on {AB} is to the rectangle {AB} by {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {AB} is incommensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB², AB·BC incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "But the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC} is commensurable with the square on {AB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB² + BC², AB² commensurable", ref: "X.15" }] },
            { text: "and twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is commensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "2 AB·BC, AB·BC commensurable", ref: "X.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB² + BC², 2 AB·BC incommensurable", ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "But {EH|EHh} equals the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EHh","AB","BC"] },
            { text: "and {HF|HFh} equals twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HFh","AB","BC"] },
            { text: "Therefore {EH|EHh} is incommensurable with {HF|HFh},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EHh","HFh"] },
            { text: "so that {DH} is also incommensurable in length with {HG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DH","HG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EH : HF = DH : HG", ref: "VI.1" },
                               { claim: "DH, HG incommensurable in length", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {DH} and {HG} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DH","HG"] },
            { text: "so that {DG} is irrational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DG irrational", ref: "X.36" }] },
            { text: "But {DE} is rational, and the rectangle contained by an irrational and a rational straight line is irrational,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DE","DG"] },
            { text: "therefore the area {DF|DFh} is irrational, and the side of the square equal to it is irrational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DFh"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DF irrational", ref: "cf. X.20" },
                               { claim: "its side irrational", ref: "X.Def.I.4" }] },
            { text: "But {AC} is the side of the square equal to {DF|DFh}, therefore {AC} is irrational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","DFh"] },
            { text: "Let it be called a second bimedial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.38") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.41":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI41/",
        "II.4":      "/elements/books/bookII/propositions/propII4/",
        "VI.1":      "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.6":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/",
        "X.11":      "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.13":      "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX13/",
        "X.15":      "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX15/",
        "X.22":      "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.36":      "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX36/",
        "cf. X.20":  "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX20/",
        "X.Def.I.4": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.I.4/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Since the square on {AC} equals the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC} and twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}, apply {EH|EHh}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC}, to {DE}. Then the remainder {HF|HFh} equals twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}. [!just II.4]

Since each of the straight lines {AB} and {BC} is medial, therefore the squares on {AB} and {BC} are also medial. But, by hypothesis, twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is also medial. And {EH|EHh} equals the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC}, while {FH|HFh} equals twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}, therefore each of the rectangles {EH|EHh} and {HF|HFh} is medial.

And they are applied to the rational straight line {DE}, therefore each of the straight lines {DH} and {HG} is rational and incommensurable in length with {DE}. [!just X.22]

Since {AB} is incommensurable in length with {BC}, and {AB} is to {BC} as the square on {AB} is to the rectangle {AB} by {BC}, therefore the square on {AB} is incommensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BC}. [!just X.11]

But the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC} is commensurable with the square on {AB}, and twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is commensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BC}. [!just X.15; X.6]

Therefore the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}. [!just X.13]

But {EH|EHh} equals the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC}, and {HF|HFh} equals twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}.

Therefore {EH|EHh} is incommensurable with {HF|HFh}, so that {DH} is also incommensurable in length with {HG}. [!just VI.1; X.11]

Therefore {DH} and {HG} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only, so that {DG} is irrational. [!just X.36]

But {DE} is rational, and the rectangle contained by an irrational and a rational straight line is irrational, therefore the area {DF|DFh} is irrational, and the side of the square equal to it is irrational. <div class="just">cf. <a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX20/">X.20</a><br><a href="/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.I.4">X.Def.I.4</a></div>

But {AC} is the side of the square equal to {DF|DFh}, therefore {AC} is irrational. Let it be called a *second bimedial* straight line.

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
